/Title (This paper provides a highly relevant architectural reference for secure, privacy-preserving user verification by combining on-chain hashing with encrypted off-chain IPFS storage to protect sensitive KYC documents. While it offers strong strategies to prevent identity fraud and mitigate vulnerabilities like borrower-recommender collusion, its scope is limited strictly to identity and data management; it does not address the core financial mechanics of P2P lending, such as credit scoring, loan default prediction, or automated lending decisions.)
